ython and it covers these standard  topics like data wrangling machine  learning supervising and unsupervised  learning feature selection signature  patterns regression deep learning and  others and uh kind of separate from the  other types of courses that we've had  this one is also focused on going  through these practical coding  challenges and generating a number of  notebooks that you can use as your own  repository of projects that you have  completed and these projects are  something that you can run and kind of  know the analysis yourself but also  anyone else can try on their own so this  is  um  you know these are just some topics that  we cover in this program that I think  are very relevant as we have more and  more complex data sets that you have to  analyze  um and that goes from kind of a high  level overview to more detailed  um kind of understanding of methods that  I think are important for anyone who is  going into this field so it's not just  high level superficial information but  actually detailed connection between the  methods the way to use those methods and  project examples where you can apply  these methods in a meaningful way and so  the way that these projects are designed  is that we take all of these Concepts  that I just went through and we actually  use uh specific Publications that  reference these key terms like here you  can see an abstract from a paper that we  actually use in the exercises and these  papers lead to an understanding of how  these methods are being being used by  experts  let me finally summarize this with who  um and how these programs are organized  and and what are the practical outcomes  that I see  so typically a program consists of three  steps first we understand the context  then we learn about bioinformatics  methods and then you have a series of  Exemplar projects that you can choose  from so that you can get started on a  project of your own  and so the full process is when we start  from basic trainin